  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Friday) \nIssued at 1225 PM MDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nMuch quieter weather will be on tap for Tuesday, as northwest flow\naloft relaxes and remains considerably drier and cooler. High\ntemperatures will remain slightly below normal on Tuesday. \n\nInto Wednesday, a mid latitude shortwave trough is projected to\ncross northern CA and move into CO, perhaps closing into low per\nthe GFS. Timing differences among deterministic models are still \nposing uncertainties, but there is fair consensus that associated \nprecipitation would stay favored near and north of the NM-CO \nborder through Wednesday and Wednesday night. Breezes would \nincrease Wednesday during the passage of the wave/low, and daytime\ntemperatures would remain seasonable.\n\nLighter west northwest flow aloft would follow on Thursday, and\nthen a baggy trough would potentially develop upstream of NM into\nAZ on Friday. This dry and essentially barotropic upper level \nfeature would slide southeastward, mostly bypassing NM into \nSaturday while a separate trough/low moves down the central \nplains. The latter feature could invoke some breezy to windy \nconditions with a cold front passage on Saturday, but otherwise \nand elsewhere temperatures look to remain within a few degrees of \nseasonal averages Thursday- Saturday along with mostly dry \nconditions.",
